(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// CPython 3.14's bytecode as a view of a code object (queue 229; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 229\"): pyi runs its"] [4 1 "// IR; co_code, co_consts, co_linetable, co_exceptiontable, co_positions, co_lines, co_stacksize and the offsets f_lasti and"] [5 1 "// tb_lasti count are this view, made from the IR the first time one of them is asked (bytecode.go: the IR as the"] [6 1 "// instructions codegen.c emits; bytecode_flow.go: flowgraph.c's passes; bytecode_asm.go: assemble.c). Each instruction keeps the IR"] [7 1 "// instruction it came from, so that an offset of the view and an instruction of the machine answer for each other."] [9 1 "// bcLoc is an instruction's location (compile.c's location): line -1 is NO_LOCATION, a column -1 none."] [14 1 "// bcInstr is cfg_instr: pc is the IR instruction it came from, -1 for none."] [21 16 "// the code unit it starts at (bytecode_asm.go)"] [24 1 "// bcBlock is basicblock."] [32 47 "// the handler's start depth, from its region's start (-1 unknown)"] [37 1 "// bcUnit is a code object on its way to the view."] [43 15 "// the IR's cell and free indices as localsplus offsets"] [45 17 "// the IR's stack depth at each instruction"] [48 1 "// irSlot is a value on the IR's stack: the instruction that made it (a merge of paths: -1 - the instruction they meet at),"] [49 1 "// and for a with statement's exit, which is two of CPython's (LOAD_SPECIAL pushes the method and self)."] [53 15 "// the lasti pyi's finally keeps (irFinally): CPython has no such value"] [54 15 "// 3.15: a for loop's iterator, two of CPython's (GET_ITER pushes the NULL index over it)"] [57 1 "// irFinally: the row is a finally's handler, entered with the lasti that CPython's has not (SETUP_FINALLY, preserve_lasti 0)."] [63 1 "// irPops is the instruction's pops and pushes on the fall-through path."] [135 1 "// bcPlan is what the IR's stack says about each instruction, for bcEmit."] [137 20 "// PUSH_NULLs before the instruction (after its label)"] [138 20 "// a load-attr that is a call's method (LOAD_ATTR's low bit)"] [139 20 "// a call's count as CALL's oparg"] [140 20 "// a pop of a with statement's exit: two POP_TOPs"] [141 20 "// a pop of irFinally's lasti: none"] [142 20 "// a store-fast of a load-fast-and-clear's value: STORE_FAST_MAYBE_NULL"] [143 20 "// a conversion before a format spec: CONVERT_VALUE where the value was finished"] [144 20 "// a call of super: 1 no arguments, 2 two; the load-attr after it LOAD_SUPER_ATTR"] [145 20 "// an instruction with nothing in CPython's (f(*a): no list)"] [146 20 "// a swap across a with's exit"] [147 2 "// 3.15 (queue 238): the NULL index over each loop's iterator, and codegen.c's places of GET_ITER"] [148 20 "// a swap's, copy's or append's oparg more by the iterators' NULLs it reaches across"] [149 20 "// an inlined comprehension's get-iter: the for-iter it goes before (+1), after the hidden locals' saves"] [150 20 "// a generator expression's load of .0: made before RETURN_GENERATOR (-1 none)"] [153 1 "// isImportOriginated is codegen.c's: name is bound by an import in the module's scope."] [176 1 "// irPlan walks the IR in order with its stack of makers: where a call's callable was finished is where codegen.c pushed"] [177 1 "// the NULL (or loaded the method)."] [184 31 "// a for-iter -> the get-iter moved before it"] [195 30 "// a list-to-tuple's list"] [196 30 "// the list-extends of a build-list"] [249 5 "// f(*a): codegen.c's ex_call passes a's value itself"] [271 25 "// the message is the slot of self: CALL 0"] [275 5 "// 3.15: a comprehension's code gets the iterable, its GET_ITER is the callee's (codegen_comprehension)"] [378 1 "// irPlan315 finds codegen.c 3.15's places of GET_ITER: an inlined comprehension's after the saves of its hidden locals and"] [379 1 "// its container (codegen_comprehension: ITERABLE_ON_STACK), a generator expression's in its own code before"] [380 1 "// RETURN_GENERATOR (ITERATOR_ON_STACK)."] [419 1 "// irAsyncForNext: the yield-from at pc awaits an async for statement's __anext__ (not a comprehension's: in a"] [420 1 "// generator expression's or a comprehension's code, or in an inlined comprehension's cleanup region)."] [439 1 "// irDeeper is the oparg 3.15 adds to a stack-reaching instruction for the NULL over each loop's iterator it reaches across."] [463 1 "// irSelfCall: a call codegen.c makes with its one argument in self's slot (CALL 0): a decorator's and a comprehension's."] [485 1 "// irClassCall: the call at pc is __build_class__'s."] [503 1 "// irSuperOK is can_optimize_super_call's conditions: a function with a first argument and a __class__ for super()."] [519 1 "// irMethodCall is maybe_optimize_method_call's conditions on what the IR keeps: the base is not imported, the arguments fit."] [550 1 "// bcBinaryOps are NB_* by the IR's BinOp."] [568 2 "// 3.15 (pycore_opcode_utils.h)"] [575 1 "// irEagerImport is 3.15's forced eager bit of IMPORT_NAME: 2 outside the module's scope, in a try statement's or a handler's"] [576 1 "// region (_PyCompile_InExceptionHandler: a with statement is not one) and for import *."] [594 1 "// bcLinear is the instruction list before it becomes blocks: first[pc] the index of IR instruction pc's first instruction,"] [595 1 "// labels the extra jump targets among the indices."] [599 15 "// an instruction's jump target, an index (-1 none)"] [600 2 "// hpc: an instruction whose handler is another IR instruction's (3.15's moved GET_ITER), or none (-2: the prefix)"] [609 1 "// irLoc is IR instruction pc's location."] [621 1 "// irConstSlice is the constant slice starting at pc: its bounds' instructions (a -N is two: ast_preprocess.c's fold_unaryop"] [622 1 "// made it a constant), and the instructions it takes, the build-slice's index; nil for none."] [639 1 "// bcEmit is the instructions codegen.c would have emitted for the IR, as far as the IR shows them."] [644 26 "// a yield-from's SEND, by its pc"] [649 26 "// a for-iter's target -> the index of its END_FOR"] [669 2 "// 3.15: the generator's prefix is codegen_enter_scope's, before RESUME, outside every handler; a generator"] [670 2 "// expression's iterator is made before it (codegen_comprehension)"] [676 4 "// LOC(outermost->iter): the loop's (the IR's load of .0 is at the expression's)"] [703 4 "// an inlined comprehension's GET_ITER, after its hidden locals and its container (in their handler's region)"] [743 26 "// 3.15: SEND's NULL under an awaitable (codegen.c, before ADD_YIELD_FROM)"] [747 5 "// codegen_slice: a slice of constants is a constant, made where its first bound would have been"] [997 4 "// a loop's back edge is JUMP, the others codegen.c's JUMP_NO_INTERRUPT (they differ when a cold block jumps back)"] [1010 30 "// 3.15: a moved one is made before its for-iter"] [1020 5 "// END_ASYNC_FOR jumps to the SEND of the __anext__ it ends (codegen_async_for: ADDOP_JUMP ... END_ASYNC_FOR, send)"] [1039 5 "// GET_ITER GET_ITER_YIELD_FROM, as _PyCode_Quicken's fixup_getiter leaves it in co_code"] [1049 4 "// the iterator and the value are below: SEND ... END_SEND (codegen_add_yield_from)"] [1069 25 "// codegen_async_for's, after the __anext__'s POP_BLOCK"] [1071 38 "// the handler of YIELD_VALUE, an index + 1, for bcBlocks"] [1120 5 "// IMPORT_NAME's name << 2 and the eager bit (codegen_import, codegen_from_import; no lazy import yet: P3)"] [1189 1 "// bcBlocks makes the blocks of the list (_PyCfg_FromInstructionSequence), each instruction's handler"] [1190 1 "// (label_exception_targets, from the IR's table) and the generator's wrapper (codegen_wrap_in_stopiteration_handler)."] [1212 2 "// the block of each index; empty blocks at leaders after the last instruction go away"] [1231 3 "// 3.15: what the prefix leaves (a generator expression's iterator) is under the handler too"] [1262 5 "// generated: the handler of the IR instruction beside it"] [1288 4 "// a jump the compiler's flow! threaded: jump_thread's new